WEBVTT

00:00:05.090 --> 00:00:07.130
It's hot, isn't it, Hana Bear?

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:09.460
It sure is, Tama Bear.

00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:13.430
I feel like having ice-cold salmon
on something slippery!

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:15.140
Like cold white noodles.

00:00:15.550 --> 00:00:17.970
Salmon flowing down the bamboo pipe
would be nice, too!

00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:21.980
Isn't that the same thing as the fish
swimming in the river as usual?

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:25.480
Swimming or flowing down a pipe.

00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:28.020
There's a major difference!

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:29.400
That's deep!

00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:31.820
Of course it's deep because it's a river!

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:33.030
Hana Bear!

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:34.160
Tama Bear!

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:38.620
U-Um...

00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:42.120
Y-Yes?

00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:46.880
H-Hiroe?

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:48.750
Hana...

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:50.340
Wh-Wh-What's wrong?

00:00:50.590 --> 00:00:51.800
What's with your clothes?

00:00:54.970 --> 00:00:55.760
Ei...

00:00:58.010 --> 00:01:02.980
Eiko!

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:35.940
I-I'm sorry, Hana...

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:38.110
for surprising you.

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:39.160
Not at all.

00:02:38.610 --> 00:02:42.580
THE SHARK'S COUSIN

00:02:39.490 --> 00:02:40.910
Do you feel a little calmer now?

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:42.580
Y-Yeah.

00:02:42.990 --> 00:02:46.960
Um, what happened
between you and Eiko?

00:02:48.460 --> 00:02:50.540
It was about my clothes.

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:52.000
Clothes?

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:53.250
Yeah.

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:14.480
<i>Right now, I'm standing
at a crossroads in my life!</i>

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:17.110
EIKO TOKURA

00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:16.780
<i>I-If I do this...</i>

00:03:17.110 --> 00:03:17.860
EIKO TOKURA
CALLING

00:03:22.450 --> 00:03:23.620
<i>Yes, Hiroe?</i>

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:24.990
<i>E-Eiko!</i>

00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:28.200
<i>I don't know if I should keep it in or out!</i>

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:28.960
<i>Excuse me?</i>

00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:33.380
<i>I'm talking about the shirt and skirt
you chose for me the other day!</i>

00:03:33.630 --> 00:03:36.760
<i>Oh, is that all? Either way is fine.</i>

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:38.210
<i>Either in or out.</i>

00:03:38.470 --> 00:03:41.340
<i>That's no help! You decide, Eiko!</i>

00:03:41.590 --> 00:03:43.550
<i>Tucked in or leave it out?</i>

00:03:44.550 --> 00:03:47.430
<i>Anyway, the best way
is the way you like it, Hiroe.</i>

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:50.480
<i>- But...
- Bye-bye!</i>

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:52.440
<i>W-Wait, Eiko!</i>

00:03:52.650 --> 00:03:54.310
<i>Inside or outside?</i>

00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:58.030
<i>Eiko!</i>

00:03:58.360 --> 00:04:02.860
I told myself I can't fail with this outfit,
and got too worked up about it.

00:04:03.570 --> 00:04:05.530
I was rude to Eiko.

00:04:05.780 --> 00:04:07.950
R-Really?

00:04:08.870 --> 00:04:12.210
Um, are you going somewhere, Hiroe?

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:13.710
Actually,

00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:17.550
I thought I'd sign up
for a summer course at a prep school.

00:04:18.550 --> 00:04:20.880
I was going to pick up
the documents today.

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:23.550
That's great! I'm proud of you, Hiroe!

00:04:24.090 --> 00:04:25.220
Hana...

00:04:25.470 --> 00:04:29.350
After all, you went from convenience stores
to more and more places,

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:31.430
and now you're finally going
to a prep school!

00:04:31.430 --> 00:04:34.190
You may be in the National High School
Baseball Tournament next year!

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:36.900
What do you think I'm aiming for?

00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:45.910
It's thanks to you
that I'm able to go outside at all, Hana.

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:49.160
Thanks so much, Hana.

00:04:49.450 --> 00:04:52.330
O-O-Oh, I didn't do anything!

00:04:52.580 --> 00:04:53.370
In fact...

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:57.590
even though you're moving forward,

00:04:57.840 --> 00:05:00.130
I feel like I'm walking in place.

00:05:00.590 --> 00:05:01.880
Hana...

00:05:02.260 --> 00:05:05.010
I know I have to tell them.

00:05:05.590 --> 00:05:08.100
It's not good to keep it hidden.

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:09.470
You mean the shirttail?

00:05:09.810 --> 00:05:10.720
No!

00:05:11.140 --> 00:05:11.930
Hana!

00:05:11.930 --> 00:05:15.310
What should I do about the bottom
of my shirt? You decide!

00:05:16.100 --> 00:05:18.730
Should I tuck it in? Or leave it out?

00:05:18.730 --> 00:05:21.740
I-I'm not good at making decisions like that.

00:05:21.740 --> 00:05:23.860
You're the only one I can count on, Hana!

00:05:24.240 --> 00:05:26.990
You decide! In or out?

00:05:30.450 --> 00:05:33.370
Hana, I ironed your uniform.

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:37.500
Help me, Shion!

00:05:36.170 --> 00:05:38.250
Oh, what's wrong?

00:05:38.750 --> 00:05:40.500
In or out?

00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:44.260
In? Or out?

00:05:41.760 --> 00:05:44.260
What's wrong with you two?

00:05:45.970 --> 00:05:47.010
Good question.

00:05:47.300 --> 00:05:49.390
I guess it's cuter tucked in.

00:05:49.720 --> 00:05:50.810
You're right.

00:05:52.220 --> 00:05:53.810
Thank you, Shion!

00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:55.730
But this shirt...

00:05:56.020 --> 00:05:57.730
The design of the bottom is cute,

00:05:58.150 --> 00:06:00.150
so maybe it's better untucked after all.

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:01.360
You're right!

00:06:01.650 --> 00:06:04.820
Sh-Shion, so which is it?

00:06:06.280 --> 00:06:07.320
Let's see.

00:06:07.570 --> 00:06:09.990
First, loosen the shirt up a bit.

00:06:09.990 --> 00:06:11.700
Make your hair like this.

00:06:12.410 --> 00:06:13.870
Maybe a hat would look good.

00:06:14.660 --> 00:06:15.830
Now hold this.

00:06:19.080 --> 00:06:20.130
It's perfect!

00:06:20.790 --> 00:06:22.300
How's this look?

00:06:22.550 --> 00:06:23.800
Shion?

00:06:24.510 --> 00:06:26.380
Eiko!

00:06:29.550 --> 00:06:31.510
Sorry for suddenly showing up.

00:06:31.810 --> 00:06:32.810
- Eiko!
- Eiko!

00:06:33.060 --> 00:06:33.930
Eiko!

00:06:33.930 --> 00:06:36.060
Yep, it's me, Eiko.

00:06:37.020 --> 00:06:41.610
I-I'm so sorry for harassing you
over the phone.

00:06:42.480 --> 00:06:47.490
Not at all. I was out shopping
with my little sister at the time.

00:06:47.860 --> 00:06:50.950
<i>Eiko! I don't know
if I should keep it in or out!</i>

00:06:50.950 --> 00:06:51.700
<i>Excuse me?</i>

00:06:52.330 --> 00:06:55.500
<i>In or out? That's a tough question.</i>

00:06:55.750 --> 00:06:57.500
<i>Either way is fine.</i>

00:06:57.830 --> 00:06:59.080
<i>Either in or out.</i>

00:06:59.080 --> 00:07:00.630
<i>That's no help!</i>

00:07:00.630 --> 00:07:02.500
<i>You decide, Eiko!</i>

00:07:02.750 --> 00:07:04.750
<i>Tucked in or leave it out?</i>

00:07:06.010 --> 00:07:09.430
<i>If it's out, it'll flap around.
Tucked in is better.</i>

00:07:09.430 --> 00:07:12.680
<i>Anyway, the best way
is the way you like it, Hiroe.</i>

00:07:13.010 --> 00:07:14.810
<i>Bye-bye!</i>

00:07:14.810 --> 00:07:17.730
<i>W-Wait, Eiko! Inside or outside?</i>

00:07:20.020 --> 00:07:22.610
Eiko, thank you so much for coming!

00:07:22.860 --> 00:07:26.320
Don't worry about it.
I was in the area anyway.

00:07:26.570 --> 00:07:28.400
There you go.

00:07:28.400 --> 00:07:32.240
With this outfit, tucked in
gives you a more balanced look.

00:07:33.950 --> 00:07:36.790
Eiko, you're fashionable,
so your opinion counts.

00:07:37.250 --> 00:07:38.750
No, I wouldn't say that.

00:07:39.080 --> 00:07:40.710
You look nice, Hiroe!

00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:42.580
Th-Thank you.

00:07:42.830 --> 00:07:46.170
I pray you can pick up
that paperwork safely.

00:07:46.420 --> 00:07:50.340
S-Sorry for making you
pray over trivial things for me.

00:07:51.470 --> 00:07:53.090
Eiko, Ms. Hannen...

00:07:53.350 --> 00:07:55.970
Why not stay over for dinner?

00:07:56.390 --> 00:07:57.350
You don't mind?

00:07:57.600 --> 00:08:00.480
I'd love to! But...

00:08:00.770 --> 00:08:03.770
my sister's making curry tonight, so...

00:08:04.810 --> 00:08:06.650
I can't blame you for going with curry!

00:08:06.650 --> 00:08:07.900
Sure, it's curry.

00:08:07.900 --> 00:08:09.280
Anyone would go with curry.

00:08:09.530 --> 00:08:13.950
For me, the main point is that my
little sister's making it, not the curry itself.

00:08:13.950 --> 00:08:17.290
A little sister's curry...
I bet it's delicious!

00:08:17.290 --> 00:08:18.580
I wish I could have some!

00:08:18.830 --> 00:08:20.330
Me, too!

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:23.580
You guys are just fixated on curry.

00:08:25.500 --> 00:08:27.170
Well, I'm off.

00:08:27.420 --> 00:08:28.340
See you!

00:08:28.590 --> 00:08:29.590
Be careful going home.

00:08:29.840 --> 00:08:32.050
Again, thank you for this, Eiko!

00:08:32.300 --> 00:08:34.050
No, it's not a big deal.

00:08:34.390 --> 00:08:35.930
Hana, can I talk to you a second?

00:08:38.810 --> 00:08:39.810
What's up?

00:08:40.640 --> 00:08:43.600
Actually, this is the real reason I came over.

00:08:44.810 --> 00:08:46.150
I'd like you to have this.

00:08:46.150 --> 00:08:47.650
F-For me?

00:08:47.650 --> 00:08:48.400
Yeah.

00:08:56.450 --> 00:08:57.740
It's beautiful!

00:08:58.030 --> 00:09:00.500
Eiko, did you...

00:09:00.750 --> 00:09:02.540
That's right, I made it.

00:09:02.870 --> 00:09:05.000
It's my thanks
for listening to me that time.

00:09:05.250 --> 00:09:07.340
Oh, you didn't need to thank me.

00:09:07.340 --> 00:09:09.460
Well, please, just accept it.

00:09:10.010 --> 00:09:12.470
I was going to give it to you
when the two of us were alone,

00:09:12.720 --> 00:09:14.800
but didn't have the chance.

00:09:15.260 --> 00:09:17.550
<i>That's because Eiko is popular.</i>

00:09:17.930 --> 00:09:20.680
I made that with you in mind, Hana.

00:09:21.310 --> 00:09:23.310
M-M-Me?

00:09:24.560 --> 00:09:26.980
The motif is a four-leaf clover.

00:09:27.690 --> 00:09:30.360
Like, "May good things happen to Hana."

00:09:31.070 --> 00:09:32.070
Eiko...

00:09:33.110 --> 00:09:36.070
Thank you, Eiko! I love it!

00:09:36.070 --> 00:09:38.070
I'm glad to hear it.

00:09:38.070 --> 00:09:39.910
I'll wear it every day!

00:09:40.160 --> 00:09:44.160
On my uniform... The teacher might
get mad, so I'll put it on my bag!

00:09:44.620 --> 00:09:47.040
But then it might break easily.

00:09:47.290 --> 00:09:49.790
Um, what should I do?

00:09:50.800 --> 00:09:52.670
Hana, you tend to overthink things.

00:09:52.920 --> 00:09:56.090
Don't think of a gift breaking
from the moment you receive it.

00:09:56.090 --> 00:09:57.930
Y-You're right.

00:09:58.390 --> 00:10:00.930
The person who made it
is always next to you,

00:10:01.260 --> 00:10:04.430
so even if it broke, just ask me to fix it.

00:10:06.060 --> 00:10:07.770
Okay! Thank you!

00:10:11.190 --> 00:10:12.530
It's cute!

00:10:13.570 --> 00:10:15.950
Eiko is amazing!

00:10:25.080 --> 00:10:27.080
HOSHIO PRIVATE GIRLS ACADEMY

00:10:28.960 --> 00:10:29.920
Whoa!

00:10:30.290 --> 00:10:31.540
S-Sorry!

00:10:32.670 --> 00:10:34.420
Oh, it's you, Ichinose.

00:10:35.010 --> 00:10:36.590
Watch where you're walking.

00:10:36.840 --> 00:10:38.640
S-Sorry.

00:10:38.640 --> 00:10:40.140
I was daydreaming...

00:10:40.390 --> 00:10:41.640
<i>Come to think of it,</i>

00:10:42.470 --> 00:10:44.680
<i>I wonder what she thinks about it.</i>

00:10:45.310 --> 00:10:49.270
<i>The fact that I've kept
my gap year secret all this time...</i>

00:10:49.520 --> 00:10:51.150
Hey, Ichinose...

00:10:51.520 --> 00:10:52.650
Y-Yes?

00:10:52.940 --> 00:10:55.780
I was just gonna buy some ice cream.
You wanna come?

00:10:56.150 --> 00:10:57.860
I'll treat you to one, but only one.

00:10:59.320 --> 00:11:03.490
Just don't tell anybody else.
They'd never let me hear the end of it.

00:11:03.830 --> 00:11:05.700
<i>That's showing favoritism!</i>

00:11:05.950 --> 00:11:07.460
<i>- Favoritism, favoritism!
- Favoritism, favoritism!</i>

00:11:07.460 --> 00:11:09.120
<i>Gimme ice cream!</i>

00:11:11.380 --> 00:11:13.210
Th-Thank you.

00:11:13.460 --> 00:11:14.920
Yeah, go ahead, eat.

00:11:19.840 --> 00:11:22.430
Teacher, is ice cream your breakfast?

00:11:22.430 --> 00:11:25.640
Yeah, I never have much of an appetite
over the summer.

00:11:26.730 --> 00:11:27.520
What?

00:11:27.770 --> 00:11:28.890
N-Nothing.

00:11:29.810 --> 00:11:31.230
Teacher...

00:11:33.480 --> 00:11:35.230
Do you, um...

00:11:36.150 --> 00:11:41.240
Do you think I should tell Eiko
and the others about my gap year?

00:11:45.990 --> 00:11:47.160
Do you wanna tell them?

00:11:47.540 --> 00:11:49.330
I don't know if I want to tell them,

00:11:50.080 --> 00:11:52.710
but I feel like it's wrong not to tell them.

00:11:52.960 --> 00:11:56.340
If it's wrong, then I would've told them
on the first day.

00:11:56.590 --> 00:11:58.470
G-Good point.

00:12:00.050 --> 00:12:02.760
Then I don't have to tell them?

00:12:03.010 --> 00:12:04.430
Of course not.

00:12:04.680 --> 00:12:07.890
Do you have to confess
your secrets to them,

00:12:07.890 --> 00:12:09.180
just because they're your friends?

00:12:10.560 --> 00:12:11.940
You do think that.

00:12:12.190 --> 00:12:13.560
You're so serious.

00:12:13.560 --> 00:12:15.400
Um, just a little.

00:12:16.610 --> 00:12:20.360
Hiding something makes me feel uneasy.

00:12:20.900 --> 00:12:25.950
At first, I thought I'd get made fun of
or teased for having a gap year,

00:12:26.200 --> 00:12:28.370
and that scared me.

00:12:30.160 --> 00:12:31.370
But now...

00:12:33.210 --> 00:12:36.460
I'm scared of having
my relationships change.

00:12:37.380 --> 00:12:39.050
Looking at it from the outside,

00:12:39.050 --> 00:12:43.430
seems to me that whether you tell them
or not, it won't change anything.

00:12:45.050 --> 00:12:47.810
Well, don't overthink it.

00:12:49.560 --> 00:12:53.600
Eiko told me the same thing.

00:12:55.270 --> 00:12:58.320
Even if we said the same thing verbatim,

00:12:58.650 --> 00:13:01.570
my words have more wisdom than hers.

00:13:01.780 --> 00:13:03.070
R-Right.

00:13:03.490 --> 00:13:05.200
The depth is different.

00:13:08.910 --> 00:13:11.370
Hana-hoo, good morning!

00:13:11.750 --> 00:13:13.210
Hoo, morning.

00:13:13.460 --> 00:13:14.960
G-Good morning!

00:13:14.960 --> 00:13:17.250
Morning! Another hot one, huh?

00:13:17.250 --> 00:13:19.000
The hottest day of summer.

00:13:19.340 --> 00:13:21.010
- The hottest?
- The hottest.

00:13:21.380 --> 00:13:23.760
All of a sudden, this is some summer!

00:13:24.010 --> 00:13:27.260
It's like, so hot it gives me the chills!

00:13:27.680 --> 00:13:30.470
That makes it sound cold, Tama.

00:13:30.470 --> 00:13:31.390
Huh?

00:13:31.980 --> 00:13:33.270
By the way, Hana...

00:13:34.060 --> 00:13:35.770
Shion told me

00:13:36.100 --> 00:13:37.650
about the gap year thing.

00:13:42.820 --> 00:13:43.990
<i>Why?</i>

00:13:44.240 --> 00:13:45.160
A gap year?

00:13:45.160 --> 00:13:47.070
Where you wore only Gap clothes for a year?

00:13:47.070 --> 00:13:48.870
Not that kind of gap year.

00:13:49.120 --> 00:13:51.490
<i>I... I...</i>

00:13:51.700 --> 00:13:53.710
Huh? Did I get it wrong?

00:13:53.710 --> 00:13:57.500
Shion said she couldn't find a full-time job
last year, so this is like her gap year.

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:01.590
Shion is having a gap year?

00:14:02.380 --> 00:14:03.920
Yeah, without working.

00:14:05.340 --> 00:14:06.130
Huh?

00:14:06.380 --> 00:14:08.470
Was I supposed to keep that to myself?

00:14:08.970 --> 00:14:11.720
You get information that not even
the person's relatives know about?

00:14:11.720 --> 00:14:13.810
Your communication gauge's
reached its max value?

00:14:14.180 --> 00:14:15.940
That's an exaggeration.

00:14:16.230 --> 00:14:19.310
We were texting each other normally
and it just came up.

00:14:19.310 --> 00:14:21.940
Texting normally... Texting?

00:14:22.320 --> 00:14:24.490
You really are on the ball, Eiko!

00:14:24.740 --> 00:14:28.320
When did you and Shion
exchange contact info?

00:14:29.160 --> 00:14:31.280
When we were at the pool,
and it just happened normally.

00:14:31.280 --> 00:14:34.950
You and your "normally"!
That's not normal at all!

00:14:34.950 --> 00:14:36.250
Big Brother Kamuri!

00:14:36.920 --> 00:14:39.040
She's getting a little big for her britches!

00:14:39.290 --> 00:14:41.170
Why don't we put her in a pickle?

00:14:41.170 --> 00:14:42.840
VINEGAR

00:14:41.750 --> 00:14:42.840
Okay, with vinegar.

00:14:42.840 --> 00:14:47.090
KELP

00:14:43.170 --> 00:14:44.130
And kelp!

00:14:44.380 --> 00:14:47.090
You're going to season and eat me?

00:14:47.680 --> 00:14:51.010
<i>I've been so focused on myself
that it never crossed my mind.</i>

00:14:51.260 --> 00:14:55.600
<i>Shion is in the middle
of an "unemployed gap year."</i>

00:14:56.310 --> 00:14:57.100
That's right.

00:14:57.480 --> 00:14:58.940
An unemployed gap year.

00:15:00.310 --> 00:15:01.730
I didn't tell you?

00:15:01.980 --> 00:15:03.900
Y-You never said...

00:15:03.900 --> 00:15:06.860
Oh, it slipped my mind.
I just forgot to tell you.

00:15:07.150 --> 00:15:09.450
Probably because when you first came here,

00:15:09.450 --> 00:15:11.240
I was so focused on learning
how to be a landlady.

00:15:11.830 --> 00:15:14.410
Remembering the collection days
for burnable trash, recyclable trash,

00:15:14.410 --> 00:15:16.250
large-sized garbage...

00:15:16.620 --> 00:15:19.960
Y-You sure put a lot of emphasis
on sorting the garbage.

00:15:19.960 --> 00:15:23.130
When you have a command of garbage,
you have command of being a landlady.

00:15:23.380 --> 00:15:24.880
I-I see.

00:15:25.210 --> 00:15:26.260
Looking back,

00:15:26.760 --> 00:15:31.390
maybe I was trying to forget my sorrow
by devoting myself as a landlady.

00:15:32.350 --> 00:15:33.510
Shion...

00:15:34.760 --> 00:15:38.390
But it doesn't bother me at all now.

00:15:38.690 --> 00:15:40.100
So don't worry!

00:15:40.100 --> 00:15:42.110
I'm not sure if that's a healthy attitude.

00:15:42.770 --> 00:15:46.900
But it's hard for me to believe
you couldn't get a job, Shion.

00:15:47.280 --> 00:15:51.360
Actually, I was offered a job
at one company, but Grandpa...

00:15:51.820 --> 00:15:54.580
<i>Are the chair cushions
at your company soft?</i>

00:15:55.490 --> 00:15:58.330
<i>What kind of fabric softener do you use
for the towels in the office kitchenette?</i>

00:15:58.710 --> 00:16:02.710
<i>Naturally you have your air conditioning
ducts cleaned annually, don't you?</i>

00:16:02.710 --> 00:16:06.300
<i>I'm worried
about my granddaughter's health!</i>

00:16:06.300 --> 00:16:07.670
<i>Grandpa!</i>

00:16:09.420 --> 00:16:12.050
You and I are his only grandchildren,

00:16:12.300 --> 00:16:14.390
so he's especially protective of us.

00:16:15.350 --> 00:16:16.180
So then...

00:16:17.600 --> 00:16:18.680
Good luck!

00:16:21.770 --> 00:16:23.270
Thank you for the food!

00:16:24.110 --> 00:16:26.110
I felt like making curry for some reason.

00:16:26.520 --> 00:16:28.360
It's gotta be curry!

00:16:28.360 --> 00:16:29.570
The good stuff!

00:16:30.900 --> 00:16:32.820
The tofu salad is delicious, too!

00:16:33.370 --> 00:16:34.200
Good.

00:16:35.280 --> 00:16:38.700
<i>I wonder what Shion's going to do
from now on?</i>

00:16:39.080 --> 00:16:41.960
<i>Will she stay on as my landlady?</i>

00:16:44.170 --> 00:16:46.040
Um, Shion...

00:16:46.290 --> 00:16:47.090
Yes?

00:16:47.670 --> 00:16:49.460
Um, tonight...

00:16:50.920 --> 00:16:54.220
Can I sleep over?

00:16:55.680 --> 00:16:56.600
Of course!

00:16:56.850 --> 00:16:58.430
Th-Thanks.

00:16:59.220 --> 00:17:01.770
Then why don't we take a bath
together after dinner?

00:17:03.140 --> 00:17:04.400
You're sleeping over, right?

00:17:04.400 --> 00:17:08.190
N-Never mind the bath, though!
I'm too embarrassed!

00:17:14.070 --> 00:17:15.620
You know what, Hana?

00:17:16.450 --> 00:17:20.500
Actually, when I heard
you were moving here last year,

00:17:20.750 --> 00:17:23.330
I bought pajamas and a futon for you.

00:17:24.330 --> 00:17:25.580
Really?

00:17:26.540 --> 00:17:29.420
I bought this for you, too.

00:17:29.420 --> 00:17:34.680
Jeez! Do you still think of me
as a three-year-old, Shion?

00:17:41.810 --> 00:17:43.560
Sh-Shion...

00:17:48.570 --> 00:17:49.940
It's just as I imagined!

00:17:50.320 --> 00:17:51.940
You look adorable!

00:17:52.320 --> 00:17:53.570
A-Adorable?

00:17:53.820 --> 00:17:55.240
This is adorable?

00:18:08.080 --> 00:18:09.420
Shion...

00:18:11.760 --> 00:18:12.630
Sorry.

00:18:13.130 --> 00:18:15.130
No, it's fine.

00:18:15.380 --> 00:18:17.340
Maybe you can't sleep
because it's not your own bed?

00:18:18.260 --> 00:18:19.140
No.

00:18:19.720 --> 00:18:21.140
Actually, um...

00:18:21.510 --> 00:18:24.020
I wanted to ask you something.

00:18:24.270 --> 00:18:25.480
Ask me something?

00:18:25.480 --> 00:18:26.520
Yeah.

00:18:26.900 --> 00:18:29.650
Are you going to continue
as the landlady here?

00:18:29.900 --> 00:18:33.690
Or are you going to give
job-hunting another try?

00:18:36.030 --> 00:18:38.740
To be honest, I'm still mulling it over.

00:18:39.700 --> 00:18:43.910
At first, all my friends
from college got jobs,

00:18:44.290 --> 00:18:47.790
and I was the only one
helping out at home, as it were.

00:18:48.960 --> 00:18:52.050
I was stressed, because it felt
like I'd been left behind.

00:18:53.710 --> 00:18:54.710
But then,

00:18:56.090 --> 00:18:59.800
as a landlady, I tried making it
so everyone felt comfortable living here,

00:19:00.510 --> 00:19:02.010
and cleaned up the common areas,

00:19:02.560 --> 00:19:04.140
and took care of the garden.

00:19:05.230 --> 00:19:08.020
I'd always enjoyed doing things like that,

00:19:08.270 --> 00:19:11.310
and at some point,
I realized that this suited me.

00:19:11.770 --> 00:19:13.230
Shion...

00:19:13.940 --> 00:19:16.240
Of course, if I got a full-time job,

00:19:16.240 --> 00:19:19.360
there would be various discoveries
and I'd meet all kinds of people.

00:19:19.700 --> 00:19:20.530
But...

00:19:21.070 --> 00:19:24.700
I like who I am now, too,
as the landlady here.

00:19:25.660 --> 00:19:26.660
Right.

00:19:28.080 --> 00:19:30.210
<i>I'm sorry about asking
for your help, Shion.</i>

00:19:30.710 --> 00:19:33.340
<i>But please take care of Hana.</i>

00:19:33.340 --> 00:19:35.090
<i>Of course, she's very welcome here!</i>

00:19:35.960 --> 00:19:38.800
<i>And I hope you also visit
sometimes, Aunt Hazuki.</i>

00:19:39.340 --> 00:19:40.760
<i>Thank you.</i>

00:19:41.220 --> 00:19:43.300
<i>I'm sure we'll have
a good time together, Hana.</i>

00:19:44.930 --> 00:19:47.230
<i>Thank you.</i>

00:19:52.110 --> 00:19:53.820
<i>I heard you like cold tofu,</i>

00:19:54.110 --> 00:19:56.570
<i>so I made all different kinds.
What do you think?</i>

00:19:57.150 --> 00:20:00.110
<i>Th-This is too much tofu.</i>

00:20:05.870 --> 00:20:08.370
<i>Maybe a little more on the left?</i>

00:20:08.620 --> 00:20:09.330
<i>Yeah.</i>

00:20:09.960 --> 00:20:12.380
<i>Um, thank you, Shion!</i>

00:20:13.750 --> 00:20:14.630
<i>Oh.</i>

00:20:17.090 --> 00:20:18.880
<i>Hana, you look cute!</i>

00:20:19.340 --> 00:20:21.630
<i>Short looks really good on you, too!</i>

00:20:22.010 --> 00:20:24.550
<i>O-Okay. Thank you.</i>

00:20:29.680 --> 00:20:31.190
<i>Did I fall asleep?</i>

00:20:32.350 --> 00:20:34.110
"Do your best, Hana."

00:20:34.730 --> 00:20:36.070
<i>Shion...</i>

00:20:41.030 --> 00:20:42.160
I feel...

00:20:42.660 --> 00:20:46.280
really lucky that you're my landlady!

00:20:46.870 --> 00:20:48.120
Hana...

00:20:50.660 --> 00:20:54.000
Maybe I will continue to be
the landlady after all.

00:20:56.540 --> 00:20:59.710
I'll be thrilled if you stay
as my landlady, Shion,

00:20:59.710 --> 00:21:01.380
but I don't want to pressure you into it!

00:21:01.720 --> 00:21:04.510
If you decide to look for a job,
you have my full support!

00:21:06.680 --> 00:21:09.850
When you think about it,
I'm having an "unemployed gap year,"

00:21:09.850 --> 00:21:12.810
Ms. Hannen is having a gap year,
and you had a gap year.

00:21:13.100 --> 00:21:16.270
It's like this apartment building
is "Gap Year Heights."

00:21:16.520 --> 00:21:18.690
My gap year is behind me!

00:21:20.240 --> 00:21:22.150
Well, why don't we get some sleep?

00:21:23.490 --> 00:21:25.660
Goodnight, Sharkie.

00:21:35.750 --> 00:21:37.090
Here's your lunch.

00:21:37.340 --> 00:21:40.090
U-Um, Shion, is this...

00:21:40.340 --> 00:21:42.170
It tastes even better the next day.

00:21:42.880 --> 00:21:44.300
So it is curry.

00:21:44.720 --> 00:21:46.050
Good! Thank you!

00:21:46.300 --> 00:21:47.390
Not at all.

00:21:49.260 --> 00:21:49.970
Huh?

00:21:50.560 --> 00:21:53.100
Cute! That's a pretty brooch!

00:21:54.190 --> 00:21:55.020
Thank you!

00:21:55.730 --> 00:21:57.480
It really suits you, Hana.

00:22:02.610 --> 00:22:04.740
- Well, I'll see you later!
- Yep!

00:22:06.820 --> 00:22:08.660
See you later, Hana!
